items: v2-lane-does-not-serve-the-content-introspection-view
paths: file:v2/runtime/std/content-plugin/src/main/scala/ssc/plugin/content/ContentNativePlugin.scala file:tests/e2e/serve-view-frontend-v2-smoke.sh file:v2/runtime/std/content-plugin/src/test/scala/ssc/plugin/content/ContentNativePluginTest.scala
scope: |
  `v2-lane-does-not-serve-the-content-introspection-view` says the v2 lane "never starts listening"
  and points at v2's `serve` path. MEASURED BEFORE CLAIMING: it never reaches `serve` —
  `bin/ssc-tools --v2 examples/content-introspection.ssc` answers
  `ssc: unbound global: contentToolkitBlock`, rc 1, and nothing runs. The gate only greps its log,
  so the line naming the cause was never read.

  The v2 native content plugin registers 15 intrinsics including `contentToolkitSection`, but NOT
  `contentToolkitBlock` — while the helper it needs, `toolkitBlockNode`, has been in that file since
  the toolkit port and is already called by the section builder. A missing registration, not a
  missing subsystem.

  TWO BLOCKERS, counted rather than assumed, because a refusal short-circuits: the second is
  `contentCurrentSection()`, which the example calls twice and which this plugin registers as a
  deliberate throw ("unavailable on native 2.1 without source-aware call identity"). Probed on its
  own: prints, then dies, rc 1. So THIS fix does not turn the gate green — it moves the failure from
  "refuses to load" to a documented limit already filed as
  `content-current-section-native-unavailable`. Saying so up front, because "fixed" would otherwise
  read as "closed".

  WIDENED to the plugin's test file BEFORE the edit: the registration needs an absent-state control
  that lives in the repo, and `V2PluginRegistry.lookupGlobal` is the thing that was empty.
next: register contentToolkitBlock, add the test rows, re-measure both blockers
